 {
  "type": "agent.message",
  "id": "m_4",
  "role": "assistant",
  "text": "The crash happened because `renderWatchlist` assumed `quotes.data` always exists, but the API returns `undefined` on the first render before any quotes arrive. I added a guard that treats missing or empty data as a loading state, so the dashboard now shows \"Waiting for quotes…\" instead of throwing. The fix is in `watchlist.js`.",
